╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_two_angle_chain                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses 24 distinct trainable parameters per repeated block: eight RY     │
│                          │ angles and sixteen RZ angles. The two RZ layers are separated only by diagonal CZ gates,  │
│                          │ so much of their flexibility is redundant. This produces 146 total parameters and 186     │
│                          │ gates despite already achieving perfect accuracy.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement uses two shared parameters per block: one global RY angle and one global  │
│                          │ RZ angle. A nearest-neighbor CZ chain retains full eight-qubit connectivity without       │
│                          │ adding trainable parameters. Because repetitions receive independent parameter copies,    │
│                          │ the overall circuit can still learn a sequence of distinct transformations while using    │
│                          │ roughly one-twelfth as many ansatz parameters. The reduced hypothesis space should        │
│                          │ preserve performance on this apparently simple task while improving parameter efficiency, │
│                          │ convergence, depth, and few-example generalization. Learning rate, iteration count,       │
│                          │ stopping thresholds, and optimizer selection are fixed by the external training loop and  │
│                          │ therefore cannot be changed here.                                                         │
