│ patch_description        │ This design compresses the successful rotation-and-entanglement pattern into a single     │
│                          │ collective trainable mode. All eight RY gates share one parameter, reducing the ansatz    │
│                          │ contribution from two parameters per repetition to one while imposing a strong symmetry   │
│                          │ prior that should improve few-shot generalization.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The CZ chain is retained for reliable global connectivity, but its commuting gates are    │
│                          │ reordered into even-edge and odd-edge matchings. This edge-colored schedule implements    │
│                          │ the same chain entangler while exposing greater parallelism and potentially reducing      │
│                          │ compiled depth. The result preserves the proven gate family and connectivity while        │
│                          │ improving parameter economy and removing the unnecessary even/odd rotational distinction. │
