│ patch_description        │ This design replaces separate collective rotations and fixed entanglers with a single     │
│                          │ parallel layer of parametrized XX interactions. Each XX gate simultaneously mixes and     │
│                          │ entangles its qubit pair, compressing the role of the prior RY–CZ stages into one         │
│                          │ operation. All four interactions share one parameter, preserving the minimum trainable    │
│                          │ parameter count while imposing a strong symmetry that should aid few-shot generalization. │
│                          │ Because the disjoint gates can execute in parallel, the ansatz substantially reduces gate │
│                          │ count and depth and may converge faster without sacrificing register-wide coverage.       │
