│ patch_name               │ compressed_collective_matching                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This design compresses the successful collective-RY and parallel-CZ pattern into a single │
│                          │ stage per ansatz block. Because the fixed architecture already repeats the block with     │
│                          │ independent parameter copies, duplicating the same shared rotation and matching inside    │
│                          │ each block is unnecessary. The resulting circuit preserves the one-parameter-per-block    │
│                          │ economy and proven entangling structure while halving the block gate count and depth      │
│                          │ relative to the earlier two-stage design. Removing the tied CRZ ring also simplifies the  │
│                          │ optimization landscape, targeting faster convergence without sacrificing the collective   │
│                          │ inductive bias that achieved perfect validation accuracy.                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
